Problem Statement:
Given an array and a target element, search for the target in the array. If it is present, return its index; otherwise, return -1.


Approach:
Start from the first element of the array.
Compare each element with the target.
If the current element is equal to the target, return its index.
If the entire array is traversed and the target is not found, return -1.


Algorithm:
Start from index 0.
For every element in the array:
    Compare the current element with the target.
    If they are equal:
        Return the current index.

If the loop finishes:
    Return -1.


C++ Code
class Solution {
public:
    int linearSearch(vector<int>& nums, int target) {

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++) {

            if (nums[i] == target)
                return i;

        }

        return -1;
    }
};


Time Complexity
Best Case: O(1)
Worst Case: O(n)
Average Case: O(n)

Space Complexity = O(1)
